scope: |
  SSC3-J4's `(bin cmp)` + `(brif)` fusion, as a PEEPHOLE in `Exec.exec` — no new opcode and
  no private flat encoding, because `exec` already holds a cursor and after J4b the pair is
  canonical and adjacent. IR, verifier, text form, round-trip gate, BridgeV2 and the charter
  untouched.

  Paths and why each: `Exec.scala` (the peephole and its `fuseCmpBr` split, which keeps `exec`
  under the inline budget the way J0c split `step`), `Main.scala` (the `--no-fuse-cmpbr` OFF
  arm, one binary two arms), `jit-gate.sh` (a NINTH identity arm — every pass in this series
  got one and each was proven to fire by planting), plus the board, the spec and the bench
  history for the measurement.
next: ninth identity arm, prove it fires, then measure
